+# Story 6.2 — Advance trigger (the modernization gate)
+
+Advance requires sustaining SLA ≥ 95% across active classes for the milestone
+window **and** modernizing all in-service legacy pipes **and** no active
+crisis. The era advances only when all three hold; an active crisis BLOCKS
+advance `[E15]`; unmodernized legacy pipes block advance. "Meet the gate → the
+era advances" — the gate is the trigger.
+
+## The gate formula
+
+The gate composes on the 6.1 seam (era_step's condition-eval replaces the
+scripted request as the trigger — the request→latch→fire mechanics pinned in
+6.1 never change; a scripted `advance` still works, gated the same way).
+
+- **Window:** `advance.milestone_window_ticks` (600 = 30s @ 20Hz — prototype
+  value; the GDD full-game assumption is ~8–12 min/era `[ASSUMPTION: prototype
+  tuning]`). The run must have traversed the window before the gate evaluates
+  (tick ≥ window) — the pre-window period is a sustain precondition, not a
+  block.
+- **SLA measure:** per ACTIVE class (the current era's roster —
+  `era_class_unlocked`), the WINDOWED delivery ratio `delivered/(delivered+
+  dropped)` over the last `milestone_window_ticks` ≥ `advance.sla_uptime_pct`
+  (95). Built on the 3.4 SLA metrics via the gate's OWN E30-style rolling ring
+  (per-tick deltas diffed from the serialized flow accumulators — DERIVED,
+  never serialized; rebuilt identically on replay, same status as health's
+  ring). E24: a class with zero completed demand in the window measures
+  nothing (neutral); at least one active class must have completed demand
+  (the vacuous-pass guard).
+- **Legacy predicate (the 6.3 seam):** a pipe is LEGACY iff its tier is below
+  the current era's NEWEST unlocked tier (`era_newest_tier`, from 6.1's era
+  infrastructure table). All in-service (alive) legacy pipes must be
+  modernized (demolish+redraw at the era's newest tier today; 6.3 owns the
+  real legacy model — draw-era tracking + decay — and replaces this predicate
+  at the documented seam). Demolished pipes are out of service and do not
+  block.
+- **Crisis (E15):** no active crisis (the 4.2 signal). An active crisis
+  blocks; the gate re-evaluates deterministically every tick, so when the
+  crisis clears (and the other conditions hold) the advance fires.
+
+**Block priority (observable):** `Era_Advance_Blocked{reason}` emits on the
+ENTER of a blocked state, deduped (never every tick). Reason priority:
+Crisis > Legacy > Sla (E15 is the headline contract and masks the quieter
+terms).
+
+## What shipped
+
+- **`core/era.odin`** — the gate (evaluated in `era_step` when
+  `advance_gate_enabled`): `era_gate_update` (the milestone-window ring),
+  `era_gate_block` (the three conditions), `era_newest_tier` /
+  `era_pipe_is_legacy` (the 6.3 seam predicate), `event_emit_advance_blocked`.
+  Disabled (the zero value) = the 6.1 mechanics byte-identical.
+- **`core/types.odin`** — `Advance_Block_Reason`, `Era_Gate_State` (derived,
+  never serialized), `Run_State.advance_gate_enabled` + `.era_gate`, event tag
+  `EVENT_TAG_ERA_ADVANCE_BLOCKED` (14).
+- **`data/balance.json` + `core/catalog.odin`** — the `advance` block
+  (milestone_window_ticks + sla_uptime_pct), fail-fast validated like its
+  siblings (missing key = load error; window 1..10000; bar 1..100).
+- **`core/serialize.odin`** — the tag-14 payload (append-only; no LOG_VERSION
+  bump — no new command).
+- **Harness** — `advance gate on` run-setup directive (threaded through
+  `Demo_Replay` live + replay; the drift-check gains the `advance_gate_flip`
+  divergence class, mirroring the growth-flip pin — the gate run-setup is
+  replay-determinate, not silently ignorable).
+- **Goldens** — `advance_fire.dem` (conditions met → fires: era 2 healthy,
+  the window elapses at 30s with 100% windowed SLA, the gate fires 2→3,
+  streaming unlocks), `advance_block_sla.dem` (a standard-pipe bottleneck
+  flooded → windowed ratio ~55% < 95% → `{Sla}`, era stays 2),
+  `advance_block_legacy.dem` (a narrow stub in service in era 2 → `{Legacy}`,
+  era stays 2). The E15 crisis block is UNIT-pinned (test table era 4 + the
+  real surge — a real-catalog crisis-block golden is impossible: the real
+  catalog's only crisis is the era-3 surge, and era 3 is the terminal era;
+  a golden would need era-4 content, out of scope).
+
+## Tests
+
+- **`core/advance_gate_test.odin`** (10 new): the fire path (healthy era 2 →
+  era 3, no block events); each block path (Sla, Legacy, and the E15 crisis
+  block — a real engine crisis defers the advance until it clears + the SLA
+  window recovers, then fires); replay identity for a gate-fired run (live vs
+  replay byte-identical); the window-not-elapsed precondition; E24
+  zero-completion neutrality (an idle network cannot vacuous-pass); last-era
+  inertness (era 3 in the real 3-era table emits nothing); a scripted request
+  under the gate still fires gated; the disabled gate keeps the 6.1
+  mechanics.
+- **`core/catalog_test.odin`** — the `advance` block's fail-fast rows (missing
+  / zero / negative / oversized window; 0 / 101% bar).
+- GWT (stories-v2 6.2) demonstrably green: fire path + every block path
+  tested.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` **10/10** (purity gates, 215 core tests, app
+  build, golden harness 40 demos + replay gate, palcheck, drift-check (271
+  mutations incl. the new advance_gate_flip class), preview-check, PP_DEBUG
+  builds, stats-check, input-parity 24/24).
+- **The deliberate re-bless** (the `advance` balance block folds into
+  catalog_hash): fold-check PASS (boot's tick-1 shift is the catalog fold
+  alone — bytes 33..40, mechanically proven); `.log.bin` re-bless header-only
+  (byte-verified: only the catalog_hash field differs, commands byte-
+  identical); T2 pixels byte-identical (zero `.png` churn); the 3 new gate
+  demos' goldens are deliberate additions. **Un-advanced demos are
+  byte-identical**: the gate is run-setup-opt-in, so every existing demo
+  without `advance gate on` keeps its sim unchanged (fold-only re-bless).
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **The gate is the trigger** (the 6.1 seam's first option: condition-eval
+  replaces the scripted request). The launchable increment is "meet the gate →
+  the era advances" — the player sustains + modernizes + avoids crises and the
+  era advances by itself. The request→latch→fire mechanics stay pinned; a
+  scripted `Cmd_Era_Advance` still works and is gated identically.
+- **Run-setup opt-in (`advance gate on`)**: mirrors health/growth. The gate is
+  a pure function of serialized state — replay re-derives it, so the flag is
+  run setup, never a log byte (the drift-check flip class pins this). Opt-in
+  keeps every pre-6.2 demo byte-identical (only the catalog fold shifts them).
+- **The gate's windowed SLA is its OWN ring, not health's**: the milestone
+  window (~8-12 min/era full-game) is a different duration than the health
+  meter's window; coupling them would tie the advance gate to the health
+  meter's tuning. Same E30 pattern, own window.
+- **Legacy predicate = tier < era's newest tier** (against 6.1's era infra
+  table): the MVP advance (2→3) requires modernizing narrows to standard; the
+  3→4 advance (full-game) requires modernizing to wide. Documented as the 6.3
+  seam — 6.3 replaces it with draw-era tracking + decay.
+- **E15 crisis block is unit-pinned, not golden**: the real catalog's only
+  crisis is the era-3 surge, and era 3 is the last era (no forward target).
+  A real-catalog crisis-block golden would require era-4 content (out of
+  scope — eras 4-6 are full-game). The unit test uses the test-table era 4 +
+  the real surge fixture (the 6.1 E14 scenario) and pins the full
+  deferral→recovery→fire arc.
+
+## Follow-ups (out of scope, named)
+
+- **6.3** — the real legacy model (draw-era tracking + decay): replaces the
+  `era_pipe_is_legacy` predicate at the documented seam; adds the tier-up
+  command.
+- **App-side advance trigger** — the gate is inert in the app (era 3 =
+  terminal); a player-facing advance rides a future era-4 slice.
