--- /dev/null
+++ b/demos/advance_block_legacy.dem
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# advance_block_legacy.dem — Story 6.2 golden: the era-advance gate BLOCKED by
+# the legacy condition (an in-service pipe below the era's newest tier). Era 2,
+# `advance gate on` (run setup — the gate is the trigger; replay re-derives it
+# from the serialized state).
+#
+# The traffic path is healthy-MODERN (standard pipes — era 2's newest tier; the
+# email res->res flow delivers at ~100%, so the SLA term cannot mask this
+# branch), BUT one extra pipe is a NARROW stub (tier 0 < standard) drawn in
+# service at ~9.2 tiles (within narrow max_span 10). The legacy predicate (the
+# 6.3 seam: a pipe is legacy iff its tier < the era's newest unlocked tier) is
+# true for that pipe, so at the milestone window's end (tick 600 = 30000ms) the
+# gate reports Era_Advance_Blocked{Legacy} and the era STAYS 2 — the block path
+# is T1-pinned (the event + the un-advanced era byte). 6.3 owns the real legacy
+# model (draw-era tracking + decay); this predicate is the documented seam.
+seed 90210
+run 70000ms
+era 2
+fixture qos
+advance gate on
+at 0ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 0ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 0ms draw 3 1 standard
+at 0ms draw 3 1 narrow
+capture at 15000ms
+capture at 60000ms
