diff --git a/demos/advance_fire.dem b/demos/advance_fire.dem
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fe83551
--- /dev/null
+++ b/demos/advance_fire.dem
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# advance_fire.dem — Story 6.2's named golden: the era-advance gate FIRES
+# (conditions met -> the era advances). The run starts in era 2 (email-only —
+# streaming is LOCKED by the era roster). `advance gate on` enables the 6.2
+# modernization gate (run setup — re-created identically on replay; the gate
+# is a pure function of serialized state, so the fire tick is replay-
+# determinate WITHOUT a logged command).
+#
+# The three conditions hold across the milestone window (600 ticks = 30s):
+#   - SLA: the healthy era-2 email flow (res->router->host over STANDARD
+#     pipes) delivers at ~100% — the windowed ratio stays above the 95% bar;
+#   - legacy: all in-service pipes are STANDARD (era 2's newest unlocked tier
+#     — no pipe is below it, so nothing is legacy);
+#   - crisis: era 2 has no crisis set-piece — no active crisis.
+# At the first tick the window has elapsed (tick 600 = 30000ms) the gate
+# passes and era_step fires era 2->3 on its own (the gate is the trigger —
+# NO scripted advance in the log). The Era_Advanced event emits, the era byte
+# flips, and era 3's unlocks load: streaming becomes available + the demand
+# signature switches (streaming content_host->res joins the plan from the
+# NEXT tick). T1 pins the fired state; the captures show email-only traffic
+# pre-advance and streaming triangles joining post-advance ("meet the gate ->
+# the era advances").
+seed 20261
+run 70000ms
+era 2
+fixture qos
+advance gate on
+at 0ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 0ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 0ms draw 3 1 standard
+at 0ms draw 4 1 standard
+capture at 15000ms
+capture at 60000ms
